menu "Audio core (modules/audio)"

    config AUDIO_LINE_IN_FITTED
        bool "A line-in ADC is fitted on the main I2S port"
        default n
        help
            The board profile wires the main port's data-in (boards/p4_player/board.json,
            i2s_a din) for two things: the PCM1808 line input of the design (docs/CONCEPT.md),
            and, since link protocol 1.9, the Bluetooth link, which the panel clocks and
            receives through that same port. A wired data-in is therefore no proof that an
            ADC is there, and the unit this firmware runs on has none.
            Off, AUX is not offered and a request for it is refused: offered, picking it
            switched the amplifier on to play a floating input. Turn it on for a unit that
            has the ADC.

endmenu
